---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const videoId = '4AEO1smpvzs';
---

<Layout title="Mike Trounce — Fundraise Readiness for Early-Stage Founders">
  <div id="top" class="hero">
    <div class="video-frame" id="video-frame" data-video-id={videoId}>
      <img
        class="video-thumb"
        src={`https://img.youtube.com/vi/${videoId}/maxresdefault.jpg`}
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
        onerror={`this.onerror=null; this.src='https://img.youtube.com/vi/${videoId}/hqdefault.jpg';`}
      />
      <button class="play-btn" id="play-btn" aria-label="Play video">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"></path></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <p class="video-caption">Click to play</p>
  </div>

  <div class="bio">
    <p>
      I&rsquo;m Mike. What I deliver is a <strong>Company Memo</strong> &mdash; one live document that
      holds the story of your company: the people, the product, the numbers, the plan. You
      can always find it, always see it, and it&rsquo;s always current. I build it with founders
      who&rsquo;ve already got some traction and who need to share the story with investors and
      new hires.
    </p>
    <div class="signature">Mike</div>
  </div>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section id="approach">
      <span class="eyebrow">What you get</span>
      <h2>Always there. Always current.</h2>
      <p>The Company Memo isn&rsquo;t a PDF that goes stale the day it&rsquo;s sent, or a deck that&rsquo;s out of date by the next round. It lives at one link. You can always find it, always open it, and what&rsquo;s there is always the current version of the truth &mdash; ready whenever an investor asks to see it.</p>
      <p>How you access it depends on you. If you&rsquo;re comfortable with GitHub, it&rsquo;s a single Markdown file in a private repo &mdash; you can see its history, and use it the way you already use dev tools. If you&rsquo;d rather not, it&rsquo;s a simple, private webpage instead. Same document, same link, either way.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="work">
      <span class="eyebrow">The process</span>
      <h2>Talk. Draft. Verify. Repeat.</h2>
      <p>This isn&rsquo;t one long interview &mdash; it&rsquo;s a loop, and the Company Memo it produces is never really finished.</p>
      <div class="work-grid">
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-a)"></div>
          <h3>We talk, in order</h3>
          <p>Around ten one-hour sessions &mdash; the story, the people, the product, the financials, the tech &mdash; each one recorded and transcribed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-b)"></div>
          <h3>Each session, an update</h3>
          <p>Every transcript updates the Company Memo directly &mdash; not a fresh write-up each time, a refinement of the one before it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-c)"></div>
          <h3>Nothing changes it unverified</h3>
          <p>I check every draft against what you actually said before it changes the Company Memo. If something&rsquo;s misunderstood, it loops back and gets corrected &mdash; it doesn&rsquo;t go out wrong.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-card">
          <div class="work-thumb" style="background:var(--illus-d)"></div>
          <h3>It doesn&rsquo;t have a finish line</h3>
          <p>The Company Memo isn&rsquo;t a deliverable you get once and file away &mdash; it&rsquo;s closer to a Wikipedia page for your company: always live, always the current version of the truth, updated as the company changes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="example">
      <span class="eyebrow">A made-up example</span>
      <h2>What actually gets caught</h2>
      <p>This case is invented, not a real client &mdash; but it&rsquo;s the kind of gap that shows up in almost every session. A founder isn&rsquo;t lying, they&rsquo;re just used to telling the story in the best possible light.</p>

      <div class="example-compare">
        <div class="example-card example-said">
          <span class="example-label">Session two, spoken</span>
          <p class="example-quote">&ldquo;We&rsquo;ve basically got Northwind Logistics as a customer &mdash; they&rsquo;re rolling us out across their whole fleet.&rdquo;</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card example-memo">
          <span class="example-label">What went in the Memo</span>
          <p class="example-quote">Northwind Logistics has committed to a paid pilot covering 12 vehicles, starting March. A full fleet rollout has been discussed as a goal &mdash; it is not signed or scheduled.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="example-note">Two sessions later, the plan had quietly shifted from an enterprise sales push to a self-serve SMB product &mdash; without ever being named as a change. The Memo doesn&rsquo;t just keep the newest version; it notes that the strategy moved, and roughly when.</p>

      <p class="example-links">
        <a href="/example-memo">See the full sample Memo as a webpage &rarr;</a>
        &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
        <a href="/fleetscope-company-memo-sample.md">See it as a raw Markdown file &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="favorites">
      <span class="eyebrow">A few things I like</span>
      <h2>Off the desk, for what it&rsquo;s worth</h2>
      <ul class="fav-list">
        <li><span><strong>The book I keep recommending:</strong> [add yours &mdash; e.g. The Mom Test]</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Podcast for the commute:</strong> [add yours]</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Tool I couldn&rsquo;t consult without:</strong> [add yours]</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>One indulgence:</strong> too much coffee</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer id="contact">
      <span class="eyebrow">Get in touch</span>
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:14px;">Got something worth building?</h2>
      <p class="contact-line">Send me a note &mdash; I read everything myself.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:16px;"><a class="contact-email" href="mailto:trounceflow@gmail.com">trounceflow@gmail.com</a></p>
      <p class="foot-note">Mike &middot; Startup Consultant &middot; Based in [add your city]</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  const frame = document.getElementById('video-frame');
  const playBtn = document.getElementById('play-btn');
  const caption = document.querySelector('.video-caption');
  if (frame && playBtn) {
    playBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const id = frame.getAttribute('data-video-id');
      const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
      iframe.src = `https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${id}?autoplay=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1&iv_load_policy=3`;
      iframe.title = 'Video';
      iframe.allow = 'autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen';
      iframe.allowFullscreen = true;
      frame.innerHTML = '';
      frame.appendChild(iframe);
      caption?.remove();
    });
  }
</script>
